# VContainer `[Inject]` Construct Methods

`Construct` (or other `[Inject]` methods) are called once by the container. Do not guard against repeated injection:

- No `if (_dependency != null)` checks before assignment
- No preliminary unsubscriptions before subscribing in `Construct`

Unsubscribe from events in `OnDestroy` (or equivalent teardown), not preemptively in `Construct`.

```csharp
// BAD
[Inject]
public void Construct(GemsSystem gemsSystem)
{
    if (_gemsSystem != null)
        _gemsSystem.OnGemCollected -= OnGemCollected;

    _gemsSystem = gemsSystem;
    _gemsSystem.OnGemCollected += OnGemCollected;
}

// GOOD
[Inject]
public void Construct(GemsSystem gemsSystem)
{
    _gemsSystem = gemsSystem;
    _gemsSystem.OnGemCollected += OnGemCollected;
}

private void OnDestroy()
{
    _gemsSystem.OnGemCollected -= OnGemCollected;
}
```

# LifetimeScope Registration

Never use `RegisterComponentInHierarchy`. Do not search the scene hierarchy from `Configure`.

Register only services and assets in `Configure` (e.g. `RegisterInstance`, `Register<T>`).

Inject scene `MonoBehaviour` dependencies via **Auto Inject Game Objects** on the `LifetimeScope` component in the Unity Inspector.

```csharp
// BAD
builder.RegisterComponentInHierarchy<GemsSpawner>();
builder.RegisterComponentInHierarchy<PlayerGemCollector>();

// GOOD — Configure
builder.RegisterInstance(_gemsBalance);
builder.Register<GemsSystem>(Lifetime.Singleton);

// GOOD — Inspector: add scene GameObjects to Auto Inject Game Objects on GameLifetimeScope
```
